From 89a63fe309f4f5fa427ef0eb67849a096cdb738e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Kudwien <daniel@netzstrategen.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 13:22:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(wpo): Add to cart submits invalid options when field
 validation throws.

Upstream patch for WooCommerce Product Options; extract into shared-patches
and re-apply after plugin updates until Barn2 ships it.

formValidation() calls checkFormValidity() outside a try/catch, from both
the submit button's click listener and the form's submit listener. An
exception escaping either one leaves preventDefault() unreached, so the
browser posts the very values the check was meant to reject. The server
then fails the request, WooCommerce does not redirect, and the page
re-renders with every field back at its default.

Two callbacks on the file upload path throw on input the plugin itself
produces. handleFileUploadRequiredValidation() parses the hidden value
input unconditionally, and the removedfile handler parses
file.xhr.response for files that never got an xhr (rejected by Dropzone's
accept check), whose request was aborted while queued or in flight, or
whose upload answered with an error page instead of JSON. The success
handler parses the value input unconditionally too, which drops the URL of
a file the preview list already shows as uploaded and makes the required
check fail on the server with no visible cause.

Parse defensively in all four places and treat a throw in the form check
as invalid rather than as consent.

Built bundles are patched by hand alongside their sources; the plugin
ships no build setup. wpo-product-table, wpo-quick-view and
wpo-restaurant-order embed the same validation module and are patched for
completeness even though this site loads none of them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
